%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2228fd33872feea429386c74dca8b01f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  gridWidth: 1
  gridHeight: 2
  limit7x7: 0
  limit5x5: 1
  limit3x3: 0
  humanScale: 3
  anvilScale: 0.25
  anvilRopeLength: 1.5
  anchorCoords:
  - {x: 0, y: 1}
  - {x: 0, y: 2}
  loadNodeCoords: {x: 1, y: 2}
  loadMass: 10000
  deadZones:
  - x: -1
    y: -1
    width: 3
    height: 2
  prebuiltBeams:
  - start: {x: 0, y: 1}
    end: {x: 1, y: 2}
  threeStarsLengthLimit: 1.1
  twoStarsLengthLimit: 50
  oneStarLengthLimit: 100
  openingDialogue:
  - 'In this first level, part of the structure has already been built for you. '
  - A structure is made up of <b>multiple beams connected by nodes</b> on the grid
    points. Nodes are pin joints that hold the ends of the beams together.
  - 'The structure is fixed to the outside world with <b>two anchor nodes</b>. An
    anchor node is stuck in place and can not be moved. '
  - Anchor nodes can be recognised by their color, as they have a <b>darker shade</b>
    than other members. They are always found at the bottom row or left-most column
    of the grid.
  - On the right side of the grid you will find the <b>load-bearing node</b>. A weight
    is attached to this node, and your goal is to <b>prevent this weight from falling</b>.
  - 'To complete this structure, you are only given one meter of steel beam as shown
    in your <b>toolbox on the bottom of your screen</b>. In future levels, you will
    get more material. '
  - You can implement a new beam using your available material by <b>drawing a line
    between two nodes on the grid</b>.
  - Once you have finished your structure, press the <b>TRUSS ME BRO</b> button to
    start simulating your structure in action.
  - "Well, get to work! Let's see what you've got and make sure I don\u2019t die!"
  - <b>I TRUSS YOU BRO!</b>
